# The Red Hand's leaders, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): 0 the job,
# 1 the built news, 2 what they make of you, each carried by a topic. Voice: mocking, casual,
# always counting. The Red Hand lies with a joke.
# Work talk explains the work (what, where, who for, the pay, the danger) before the accept.

conv redhand.leader.work_owed
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
when need:revenge
topic "Who owes the book?"
prio ask
voice redhand

bind took = news:lost_by(redhand)

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? stronghold :: Somebody's been taking from us and not writing it down. That's the one thing you don't do on my roads.
  say? trait:greedy :: Pay first, then the job. No, wait. Job first. I'm in a generous mood, and it won't last.
  say Somebody owes. The book says so, and the book is never wrong. People are wrong about the book all the time, right up until it's read to them.
  say? bound:took :: They took {bind:took} off us. Took it, like a coat off a hook, and they think we've forgotten.
  say So there's a line in red now, and red lines get settled. That's not anger. That's bookkeeping.
  > @who Whose line is in red? -> who
  > @why Why not let it go? -> letgo
  > @cut What's my cut? -> cut
  > @excon Settle it, or kill for it? Say which. -> straight   if bg:excon,raider
  > @help I could help you settle it. -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node who
  say? feud:bastion :: Bastion. It's always Bastion. They think a uniform is a receipt.
  say? feud:haven :: The Haven. Sweet people. They'd steal your boots and leave a thank-you note in them.
  say Whoever it is, they've got a page now. Pages get read out, one way or another.
  > @help2 Then let me read it to them. -> offer
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node letgo
  say Let it go? A road where you let things go is a road where everybody stops paying. Then the crews stop paying the boss, and we're just men with shotguns on a lorry.
  say? stronghold :: I knew a man who let people pay later. He had a garage. Ask the crews how that went for him.
  > @help3 Fine. What do you need? -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node cut
  say? trait:greedy :: Your cut is what I say it is, and I'm generous on Tuesdays. Is it Tuesday? Nobody knows any more. Let's say it is.
  say Red Hand Favor, which buys what you can't find in a cupboard. Fuel. And a line in the book that says you're useful. Useful people don't get pages.
  > @help4 Deal. What's the job? -> offer
  > @dry4 I'll take Tuesday's rate. -> offer   dry
  > @back3 Let me think about it. -> hub

node straight
  say Settling is getting it back. Killing is what happens when people won't give it back. Most give it back. You'd be amazed how reasonable people get.
  say You've done time. You know the difference. Good. Fewer mess-ups, fewer bodies to explain to the boss.
  > @help5 Then I'll settle it. -> offer
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node offer
  say Here's the job, roughly. Somebody's got something of ours, or owes for something they took. You go where they are and you collect. Collect, not kill, unless they insist.
  say It pays Favor and a cut, and it puts you in the book on the right side. They'll have guns, and they'll know you're coming. Everybody knows we come.
  > @take Deal. I'll collect for you. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @risk Who would I be up against? -> risk
  > @later Let me think about it. -> hub

node risk
  say Depends who's in red this week. Bastion shoots straight and keeps a list. The Haven barely shoots, then cries about it on the radio. Other crews shoot first and sell you after.
  say Whoever it is, don't do it near a house with kids in. That's not a rule. It's just bad for business.
  > @take4 Fine. I'm in. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later4 Not today, then. -> hub

node other_route
  say You backed another crew for the cure. Bold. The book noticed. The book also likes a freelancer, and the work pays the same.
  > @take2 Then you've still got work for me? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say? cure_held:redhand :: We've got the cure. Everybody wants a dose, and everybody's suddenly very polite to me. I could get used to it.
  say The cure's out. People still owe. The book doesn't care about medicine, and leaving is going to cost somebody something.
  > @take3 Then I'll still collect for you. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv redhand.leader.work
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
when !need:revenge
topic "What's worth the fuel?"
prio ask
voice redhand

bind truck = supply:truck

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? need:food :: Food. The lads are eating the paint off the trucks. Not really. Mostly not really. Tins, anything with a date on it that hasn't passed.
  say? need:supplies :: Fuel, parts, anything with a battery in it. A road runs on things that break, and nothing new comes in over the line.
  say? need:people :: Hands. We've more trucks than drivers. The drivers had opinions about the road, and the road had opinions back.
  say Everything's worth the fuel if you can sell it after. That's the whole economy of the Zone, and we're the only ones honest enough to say so.
  say? supply:road & bound:truck :: There's a truck of ours on its way to {bind:truck}. Our truck. Nobody touches our truck.
  say? night :: It's night. Night's for counting, day's for collecting, and you've caught me counting.
  say So. What's your question, and what's it worth to you?
  > @toll How's the toll doing? -> toll
  > @bastion What's your problem with Bastion? -> bastion
  > @press What aren't you telling me? -> told | joke | joke   check persuade redhand 2 harder:paranoid bg:excon,raider
  > @help Got any work for me? -> offer
  > @no Not today. -> hub

node toll
  say? holds:redhand>=4 :: Lovely. We've roads everywhere now. Everybody pays a bit, and a bit adds up. Tins, fuel, the odd watch off a wrist.
  say Steady. Tins, fuel, something worth knowing. Bastion paid us in bullets once, through the windscreen. We counted it as a tip.
  > @help2 I could help it add up. -> offer
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node bastion
  say? truce:bastion :: We've a truce just now. A truce is when we both agree to steal from other people for a while.
  say They think the road belongs to whoever has the flag. We think it belongs to whoever's standing on it. They've got more flags. We've got more road.
  say Kill one of theirs and every soldier in the Zone is at your door, so we don't. We sell them the man who did instead. Everybody wins except him.
  > @help3 Then let me help you keep the road. -> offer
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node told
  say? supply:lost :: We lost a truck yesterday. Not robbed. Lost. That's worse. Robbed, you know who to visit.
  say The book's short this week. Short books make the boss nervous, and the boss nervous makes everyone nervous, right down to the lads on the roadblocks.
  do learn:redhand.book_short:6h
  > @help4 Then let me fill a line. -> offer
  > @back3 Good to know. Something else. -> hub

node joke
  say I'm not telling you that I've got a secret. That's the secret. Now you know nothing, efficiently.
  > @help5 Then give me work instead. -> offer
  > @back4 Fine. Something else. -> hub

node offer
  say Got a few things. Goods to carry to a fence two towns over. A car somebody isn't using. A pharmacy to hold while the lads load up. Some honest, some honest-ish.
  say It pays Favor and a cut of whatever moves. Bastion shoots at people doing it, and so does the Haven, when it remembers how. Pick one before I change my mind.
  > @take I'm in. Show me the job. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later Let me think about it. -> hub

node other_route
  say You backed another crew for the cure. The book noticed. The book also likes a freelancer, and the work pays the same.
  > @take2 Then you've still got work for me? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node after
  say The cure's out. The road's still a road, and somebody still has to stand on it with a hand out. Everybody wants to settle up before processing.
  > @take3 Then I'll keep working for you. -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

# The Red Hand on a holding it lost: it was sold, ha (a joke lie). The truth is said by people who
# watched it go (~truth:gossip.sold@lost). And on a burning: the Red Hand didn't burn it, that's waste
# (~truth:gossip.burned@burned, the truth to a Haven house's rumour).
conv redhand.leader.news
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
topic "What's going round?"
prio world
voice redhand

bind lost = news:lost_by(redhand)
bind burned = news:burned
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by
bind from = news:taken_from
bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind truck = news:truck

node start
  jump news:lost_by(redhand) -> lost
  jump news:burned -> burned
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:taken -> taken
  jump news:truck -> truck
  say? epilogue :: Everybody's leaving, eventually. Lovely time for the book. People settle up when they're leaving, or they try to sneak off, which is better.
  say? major:book :: The book's getting balanced. Settling day's coming, and everybody's suddenly very honest with me.
  say? cure>=75 :: The beaks are close to the cure. Close is when people start offering me things.
  say Nothing much. Somebody's dog got married. Somebody's cousin got bitten. The Haven's short of tins again. The usual.
  > @mine What's going round about me? -> me
  > @more Anything else on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back0 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node lost
  say {bind:lost}? We sold it. Good price, too. Bastion paid in apologies. We've got loads of those now. ~lie:gossip.sold@lost
  > @catch Sold it? You were thrown out. -> caught   callout gossip.sold@lost
  > @more1 What else is on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node caught
  say Thrown out is a strong word. We were encouraged to leave. With guns. Fine. It's on a page. Somebody's page, and it isn't mine.
  > @more2 What else is on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node burned
  say {bind:burned} burned. Not us. Burning's waste. You can't toll a pile of ash. ~truth:gossip.burned@burned
  say Whoever lit it didn't do the sums. Ask the Haven. They'll say it was us. They say everything was us.
  > @more3 What else is on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node dead
  say {bind:dead} is dead. Shame. Owed us two drums of diesel. Death's a terrible way to settle up.
  say? trait:ruthless :: Next one in the chair inherits the debt. The book's very clear on that.
  > @more4 What else is on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node taken
  say {bind:who} took {bind:took} off {bind:from}. Good for them. Worse for whoever's paying them a toll now.
  > @more5 What else is on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node truck
  say A truck didn't make it to {bind:truck}. Wasn't us. If it was us, it'd have made it. To us.
  > @more6 What else is on the road? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back6 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  say? crew :: They call you {crew}. Cheerfully. In front of people. That's how you know they mean it.
  say? best:redhand :: That you {best}. The lads tell it round the fire. It gets bigger every time.
  say Nothing yet. Nothing's a price too. It's a cheap one.
  > @back7 Good. Let me ask something else. -> hub

node me_colours
  say That you walk round in other people's colours. The lads have a bet on whose you'll wear next.
  > @back8 Let me ask something else. -> hub

conv redhand.leader.me
for stronghold:redhand, seat:redhand/crew_boss
topic "What does the crew call me?"
prio reaction
voice redhand

node start
  jump kit:other -> colours
  jump bite_shown -> bitten
  jump kills:redhand>=2 -> killer
  jump crew -> named
  jump tier:redhand>=known -> known
  say? fresh :: Fresh. Like a loaf. We don't toll loaves. Give us time.
  say Nothing. You haven't done anything worth a name yet. The crew picks names, usually after something you'd rather they forgot. Give it a week.
  > @more What's on my page, then? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @fair Fair. -> hub

node colours
  say? kit:own :: Our colours, on you. Brave or stupid. The lads haven't decided, so they're taking bets.
  say Someone else's colours on my road. Either you robbed them or you're one of them. Both cost, different prices.
  > @more1 And what's on my page? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node bitten
  say Got a bite on you. I can count, love. That's my whole job.
  say Get to a house and declare it before you get interesting. Or there's the cut dose at our market. Works half the time. Interesting is bad for business.
  > @more2 Am I still good for business? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 I'll get it seen to. -> hub

node killer
  say {kills} of ours. Each one's a line in the book. You've got more lines than some of the lads.
  say I'm talking because talking's cheaper than shooting. Today.
  > @more3 Then read me my page. -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node named
  say {crew}. They say it like it's a joke. It is. It's also a receipt.
  say? best:redhand :: You {best}. The lads tell it round the fire.
  > @more4 And the rest of the page? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back4 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node known
  say? jobs:redhand>=3 :: Three jobs. Four? The book knows. I'd have to look. I don't have to look.
  say Known. Useful, maybe. The lads nod at you on the road. A nod's not a name, but it's not a toll either.
  > @more5 And the rest of it? -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back5 Let me ask something else. -> hub
